{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqh7u46ct3u","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"APPROVE: Codex + Cursor agentic-cli providers (task 22)","summary":"Single-attempt code-judge APPROVED impl 22 (commit c725619) and merged attempt into orch/feature/pluggable-backend (merge head 8a5ab33, --no-ff, no conflict). Verified: both codexProvider + cursorProvider are kind 'agentic-cli', registered, and implement resolveBin/isAvailable/isAuthed/buildInvocation/parseResult mirroring claudeProvider; parseResult returns the same {result,usage,raw} shape (explicit parity test asserts it). Codex argv = `codex exec --model <m> --json --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox [--add-dir]... <prompt>`; Cursor argv = `cursor-agent -p <prompt> --output-format json --force [--model <m>]` — both plausible headless invocations matching the cited docs and the Claude --dangerously-skip-permissions semantics. Graceful absence holds: not-installed CLI resolves to bare name and isAvailable returns false without throwing (resolveCliOnPath swallows the spawnSync failure); CODEX_BIN/CURSOR_BIN overrides work. getActiveBackend selects each by overlay.config.backend.provider id. Cross-platform bin resolution uses where/which like resolveClaudeBin. Scope disciplined: only lib/llm-backend.js (+288) and test/llm-backend.test.js (+263/-1) touched; dashboard, API/OpenRouter path, Claude provider, drain routing untouched (drains resolve providers generically). Tests 46/46 (13 new) green in the attempt worktree; node --check clean on both files. Intentional documented divergence from Claude: Codex/Cursor isAvailable returns false (not true) on the bare-name fallback — this IS the required not-installed contract, not a parity defect.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T22:30:38.244Z","vec":[-0.11344221979379654,-0.027455182746052742,-0.03512971103191376,-0.044350408017635345,0.014655730687081814,-0.07452905923128128,-0.04623411223292351,0.060692936182022095,-0.01187648344784975,0.02445324696600437,0